# Build System Improvement Plan

## Goal Description
Enhance the build system to ensure zero stale builds and correct sequential operations. This involves updating [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) to support a full clean build and verifying [CMakeLists.txt](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/CMakeLists.txt) dependencies.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) script will be updated to default to a "clean" build for the `autogen` folders, but we might want to add a flag for a **full** clean (removing the entire `build` directory) to guarantee no stale CMake cache artifacts.

## Proposed Changes

### Build Scripts
#### [MODIFY] [build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1)
- Add a `-Clean` switch to optionally remove the entire `build` directory.
- Ensure `taskkill` waits for the process to actually exit.
- Explicitly check for CMake errors at each step.

### CMake Configuration
#### [MODIFY] [CMakeLists.txt](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/CMakeLists.txt)
- (Optional) Ensure `libraw` dependency is correctly linked and included. (Already verified, but will double check if any other defines are needed).

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run [.\build.ps1](file:///d:/Dev/antigravity/build.ps1) and verify it builds successfully.
- Run `.\build.ps1 -Clean` (if implemented) and verify it re-configures from scratch.
- Verify the application runs after build.
